benefits of C++:
 
- fast language
- commonly used in advanced graphics apps (anything graphics intensive)
- used in embedded systems
- used a lot in video games
- C++ is more a middle level language (high level languages correlate more to human language while low level languages
tend to resemble hardware instructions)
- high level langs like java, python, and C# are much easier to understand, but are slower than low level langs
- middle/low level langs are harder to understand/write, but are very fast and works closely with machine hardware

What you're gonna need
- text editor (using VSCode)
- compiler - parses source code into machine instructions (using Windows, most likely gonna use GCC)